// Two §10.2 sentences that only bite together:
//
//   "more than one `default_discipline directive can be in force
//    simultaneously, provided each differs in qualifier"
//   "There is a precedence of compiler directives; the more specific directives
//    have higher precedence over general directives."
//
// So the qualifier is not decoration on a single global default — it SELECTS
// which nets a default claims, and two defaults with different qualifiers
// coexist rather than superseding one another. Syntax 10-1 fixes the fifteen
// legal qualifiers; `wire` and `reg` are two of them.
//
// 02 already writes a qualifier, but it picks `real` precisely because nothing
// in the module is a real net, so all 02 can show is that the qualifier PARSES.
// The discriminating arrangement needs a second directive that MUST NOT apply:
// p and n are ports with no discipline declaration, hence nets of the default
// nettype `wire` (IEEE Std 1364 §3.5), so the wire-qualified directive claims
// them and the reg-qualified one does not. A tool that ignores qualifiers and
// takes last-wins hands them ddiscrete, and V() — the potential access of the
// electrical nature, §3.6.1 — has nothing to resolve against.
//
// The oracle is §1.3.1 again: 0.75 - 0.25 = 0.5 V, exact in binary64.
//
// No `reg` net is declared, deliberately. The rule under test is that the
// reg-qualified default does NOT reach the wire nets, which needs no reg net to
// exist; adding one would only make the file depend on how VerA models a `reg`
// (as one §3.2 integer variable, LRM 7.3.1 Table 7-1's own mapping, and not as a
// net a discipline can be defaulted onto at all) — which has nothing to do with
// chapter 10.
//
// Like 41, this file discriminates: swap the two qualifiers and VerA hands the
// wire nets `ddiscrete`, whose §3.6.2.2 domain binds no nature, and `V(p, n)`
// becomes E0501 with nothing to access. Last-wins would do the same.
//
//! lrm 10.2
//! bias V(p) = 0.75, V(n) = 0.25
`default_discipline electrical wire
`default_discipline ddiscrete reg
`include "check.vh"
module ch10_default_discipline_two_qualifiers(p, n);
  inout p, n;
  analog begin
    `CHECKX("the wire-qualified default supplies electrical", V(p, n), 0.5);
    I(p, n) <+ V(p, n);
  end
endmodule
